AB  - The proceedings contain 28 papers from the Proceedings of SPIE: Instruments, Methods, and Missions for Astrobiology VIII. The topics discussed include: indigenous microfossils in carbonaceous meteorites; sample size/response relationship as a means of discriminating biotic and abiotic signatures; microbial remains in middle proterozoic rocks of northern Australia; complexes of ribose with silicates, borates, and calcium: implications to astrobiology; astrobiology of comets; testing the role of silicic acid and bio-organic materials in the formation of rock coatings; a planetary quarantine laboratory on the moon; and salt-tolerant and high-pH-resistant hydrogenase from the haloalkaliphilic sulfate-reducing bacterium desulfonatronum thiodismutans.
