AB  - Honey is one of the most valued natural products, a natural product of honey bees, formed from the nectar of flowers. In the composition of bee honey, they include B vitamins, calcium, copper, iron, zinc, etc. According to the national regulation on the quality of honey, there are basic parameters that it must meet to be called `real`. The article proposes a method for rapid assessment of key quality indicators of honey, including heavy metal content - arsenic (As), cadmium (Cd), lead (Pb), iron (Fe), mercury (Hg), as well as indicators such as pH, reducing sugars, sweet disaccharide and water content. The method is based on color image analysis and numerical mathematical models for prediction. The 29 honey samples were previously analyzed, and the values of the specified indicators were obtained. Nine digital mathematical models have been developed to evaluate quality indicators. The accuracy of the models is evaluated. Neural networks show the highest prediction accuracy. The developed models will be integrated into a mobile device for rapid assessment of copper quality.  © 2025 IEEE.
